    RELEASE-LORE-007: releng lane workdir is now a real git worktree
    
    The scheduler hands the lore-releng lane /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/releng-lane/lore,
    which was a board-only stand-in: `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` exited 128, so every
    releng tick had to hunt for /home/kara/get-h3/lore before it could read history, tags
    or remote refs.
    
    Fix (host-level, outside the repository): the stand-in was archived and replaced with a
    registered worktree of get-h3/lore on branch lane/releng-workdir (tracking origin/main).
    A separate worktree rather than a symlink keeps release probes off the foreman's
    checkout, where harness residue would stop every dry-run at "working tree dirty".
    
    Verified from the lane path itself: rev-parse --show-toplevel -> 0, remote names
    get-h3/lore, `worktree list` registers the path, and scripts/release.sh --dry-run
    answers from the same object store (clean tree, CI on HEAD 72adb69, version 0.2.0,
    tag v0.2.0 already exists).
    
